# [K57FIX] THE THREE-LEG SIBLING OF `prose_dedent.rxtin`: the SAME
# shallow-continuation shape, at BLOCK scope (a pattern block's own
# `description`) rather than the file's head, so all three parsers reach
# it — legs B (`tests/harness/run.sh`'s `prose_take`) and C
# (`tests/harness/verify_rxt.py`'s prose-region arm) carry the identical
# byte-count dedent K57 named in leg A, and this is what makes that
# reachable and REFUSED rather than merely present-but-unexercised. All
# three refuse, class value-shape, naming the shallower line's own depth
# and the depth the first continuation line set.
pattern a+
description |
    line one at four
  line two at two
    line three at four
m "aaa" 0 3
